{'question': {':question/id': '0be82a13-9498-51c9-846b-4675af17446e', ':question/problem': 'Consider the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+3z &=3 \\\\ -x+3y &=3 \\\\ -2x-6z &=-6\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form.', ':question/worked-solution': 'The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & 3 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 3 & 0 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 0 & -6 & -6\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nTransforming $M$ to reduced row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & 3 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 3 & 0 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 0 & -6 & -6\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & 3 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 3 & 6 \\\\ -2 & 0 & -6 & -6\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & 3 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 3 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & 3 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$', ':question/difficulty': ':question.difficulty/hard', ':question/answer-fields': [{':answer-field/id': '51f95c8f-89fa-5766-846a-d1729368544f', ':answer-field/key': 'selection', ':answer-field/type': ':answer-field.type/radio', ':answer-field/choices': [{':answer/id': '99411fef-9670-5aa8-b3df-57c97d7fe14f', ':answer/type': ':answer.type/math', ':answer/value': '\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 3 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}'}, {':answer/id': 'a66f362d-81d0-522b-ae83-65e2b62d4b63', ':answer/type': ':answer.type/math', ':answer/value': '\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 3 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}'}, {':answer/id': '7ce7213e-69e0-57fd-ad54-ddd8d659d7b6', ':answer/type': ':answer.type/math', ':answer/value': '\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 3 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}'}, {':answer/id': '5565fd4d-b7fd-5afd-8c00-cf4a467281d5', ':answer/type': ':answer.type/math', ':answer/value': '\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 3 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}'}, {':answer/id': 'd424fed4-9dac-50ec-9382-587618fa4a01', ':answer/type': ':answer.type/math', ':answer/value': '\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 3 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}'}], ':answer-field/correct': [':answer/id', 'a66f362d-81d0-522b-ae83-65e2b62d4b63']}]}, 'knowledge_point': {'id': 'b010a518-7aa3-5b53-9a6d-ef0779ff0dfa', 'db_id': 17592186096745, 'title': 'Finding the Reduced Row Echelon Form of a Singular 3x3 System With Two Pivots'}, 'generation': {'generator_id': '2e9ff447-ce56-57e5-9148-e9e03cc0f3aa', 'version': 'two-pivot-affine-v2', 'source_question': 'c0791632-977c-5714-8eb6-2845fc127f35', 'source_db_id': 17592186642366, 'source_basis': 5370, 'dependencies': {'sympy': '1.14.0'}, 'mathematical_fingerprint': 'b542569342dba368b1d08c69edc5434cfb3ec6fd4dd6f9e878b4d454cf899611', 'seed': 0, 'template': 'q-131634', 'profile': 'q-131634', 'replay': True, 'parameters': {'original_parameters': True}, 'math_format': 'course-academy-tex-v1'}}
